  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 55,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 312.0, 193.429, 564.516, 318.37 ],
    "font" : "MyriadPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.0,
    "text color" : "[0.10201, 0.09019, 0.0941]",
    "content" : "The Town Commission has approved renovations and new landscaping for two major parking lots in the downtown Surfside district. The ﬁ rst is the Abbott lot between 95th and 96th Streets (west of Harding Avenue behind the CVS and Flanigan’s). The other is the 94th Street lot (on the southeast corner of 94th and Harding Avenue). Contractors Lynx Construction and Luke’s Landscaping will be working with Public Works to complete the renovation. The project is scheduled to begin before the end of August."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 57,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 41.5, 238.0, 278.395, 257.176 ],
    "font" : "MyriadPro-SemiboldCond",
    "font size" : 17.0,
    "text color" : "[0.1216, 0.149, 0.498]",
    "content" : "Business Improvement District in Planning"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 46,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 41.5, 108.5, 286.195, 233.441 ],
    "font" : "MyriadPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.0,
    "text color" : "[0.10201, 0.09019, 0.0941]",
    "content" : "On July 17th a public meeting was held to discuss the possibility of creating a Business Improvement District (BID) for Downtown Surfside. Redevelopment Management Associates (RMA) presented information on how BIDs work and described possible BID programs for Downtown Surfside. Similar to a Homeowners Association, but for commercial properties, a BID formalizes a process for property and business owners to work together to improve a commercial district."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H3",
    "id" : 52,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 312.0, 170.63, 559.752, 190.934 ],
    "heading level" : 3,
    "font" : "MyriadPro-SemiboldCond",
    "font size" : 18.0,
    "text color" : "[0.1216, 0.149, 0.498]",
    "content" : "Streetscape Improvement Takes Next Step"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 53,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 312.0, 102.63, 565.704, 165.071 ],
    "font" : "MyriadPro-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.0,
    "text color" : "[0.10201, 0.09019, 0.0941]",
    "content" : "The plans for the Harding Avenue Streetscape are now being reviewed by the Florida Department of Transportation, since Harding Avenue is a state-owned street. The Town is planning to start the project as soon as it is approved by the Florida DOT."
  }, {
